This repository stores no model weights. A locally built Docker image bundles
the models below, converted to ONNX by Katsuya Hyodo (PINTO_model_zoo,
https://github.com/PINTO0309/PINTO_model_zoo). Each section lists the model,
where it comes from, its license, and the terms of what it derives from.
Review these before redistributing a built image.

1. DEIMv2-Wholebody49 (person/face detector)
   Source:  PINTO_model_zoo 488_DEIMv2-Wholebody49
   License: Apache-2.0 (model zoo catalog)
   Derived from, with their own terms:
   - DEIMv2 License, non-commercial purposes only:
     https://github.com/Intellindust-AI-Lab/DEIMv2/blob/master/LICENSE.md
   - DINOv3 License (variants s and x only):
     https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3/blob/main/LICENSE.md
   The DEIMv2 non-commercial condition applies to this model only.

2. OSNet-AIN x1.0 unified_aug (person ReID; osnet_ain_x1_0_p_unified_aug_n.onnx)
   Source:  PINTO_model_zoo 502_PersonViT (its LICENSE is Apache-2.0)
   License: Apache-2.0 (502_PersonViT/LICENSE)
   Derived from:
   - OSNet-AIN architecture, Torchreid (deep-person-reid), MIT:
     https://github.com/KaiyangZhou/deep-person-reid
   - PersonViT (hustvl), Apache-2.0:
     https://github.com/hustvl/PersonViT
   Not confirmed: the licenses of the person ReID datasets behind "unified_aug"
   (the 502_PersonViT README does not state them).

3. LVFace-T Glint360K (face recognition; LVFace-T_Glint360K.onnx)
   Source:  PINTO_model_zoo 483_LVFace (its LICENSE is MIT, ByteDance)
   License: MIT for the code. The upstream README
            (https://github.com/bytedance/LVFace#license) also says the models
            downloaded from its repo are "for non-commercial research purposes
            only". This contradicts the MIT wording in the same paragraph, so
            treat the weights as non-commercial research use until clarified.
   Training data: Glint360K (insightface). The insightface dataset README does
            not state a license for it; its terms are not confirmed.
